== paired, against the twin
  matched (prefix): delta -0.0228 (twin minus cell, so cell WORSE than twin)  SE 0.0017  z -13.7  n 164
    pre-registered rule: |delta| 0.0228 vs 2*SE 0.0033 -> PASSES the 2-SE bar
  mismatch (causal): delta +0.0031 (twin minus cell, so cell BETTER than twin)  SE 0.0006  z +5.5  n 164
    pre-registered rule: |delta| 0.0031 vs 2*SE 0.0011 -> PASSES the 2-SE bar

== per-item count (separate measurement, not from paired_se)
  matched (prefix): 151/164 items worse than the twin
  mismatch (causal): 38/164 items worse than the twin
  The rule needs the item count to AGREE with the paired delta's direction: a mean that improves while most items get worse is a few large items, not the intervention.
